# While body binding does not escape

Verifies a binding declared inside a `while` body is scoped to that body: using
the name after the loop fails with the standard undefined-variable diagnostic.

>>> source
while (false) {
    let local: int = 1
}

print(local)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: unknown binding `local` at Span { start: 48, end: 53 }

<<< exit
1
